# Service-account private keys. Nothing here needs one committed, and the
# consequence of one slipping through is worse than any other secret in this
# list: an adminsdk key is NON-EXPIRING full admin on prod Firestore, Auth and
# Storage, and the Admin SDK bypasses `firestore.rules` entirely.
#
# The `functions/scripts/` runbooks tell an operator to point
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS at exactly such a file, so one lands on a dev
# machine every time a backfill or audit is run. Until 2026-08-30 no pattern
# here would have caught it — `*google-services.json` above does not match the
# `<project>-firebase-adminsdk-<hash>.json` the console downloads.
# Keep such a key OUTSIDE the repo anyway; this is the backstop, not the plan.
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
*-service-account*.json
service-account*.json
# ...but the jest FIXTURES are fake keys and must stay tracked. The patterns
# above match `fake-service-account.json`, and that file is only safe today
# because it is ALREADY tracked — `.gitignore` cannot un-track anything. A NEW
# fixture, or a fresh clone that re-added one, would be dropped silently.
# Verified with `git check-ignore -v --no-index`, never `git status`: the
# tracked copy reports "not ignored" from `git status`'s point of view, which
# is exactly how this hides.
!**/__tests__/fixtures/*service-account*.json

# Node tooling (root + functions/)
node_modules/

# CLAUDE.md files are SHARED across machines (private repo, Windows + Mac) —
# never ignore them. A bare `CLAUDE.md` pattern matches at EVERY depth, so it
# silently drops each new nested file. Machine-local notes go in CLAUDE.local.md.
CLAUDE.local.md
**/CLAUDE.local.md
