# .claude/ is SHARED (private repo, Windows + Mac): rules, skills, agents,
# commands, hooks and settings.json must reach both machines. Only
# machine-local files stay ignored.
#
# These patterns were in .git/info/exclude, which is NOT committed — so on the
# Mac clone none of them were ignored at all, and a worktree or an agent
# registry created there was untracked-and-visible and one `git add .` away
# from being committed into the shared .claude/. This repo has been bitten by
# exactly that class of bug twice (a bare `CLAUDE.md` pattern matching at every
# depth; a merge resurrecting android/ with a live Maps key). Machine-local
# runtime state belongs here where both clones see the rule.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/checkpoints/
.claude/mailbox/
.claude/routines/.state/
.claude/agent-registry.json
.claude/agent-memory-local/
.claude/first-run
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
.claude/assistant-daemon-state.json
.superpowers/
superpowers/
docs/superpowers/

